          "type": "mc",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "stem": "If P(x)=3x³−7x²+2x+4, divide P(x) by x−3. Give your answer in the form P(x)=Q(x)(x−3)+R(x).",
          "options": [
            "P(x)=(3x²+2x+8)(x−3)+28",
            "P(x)=(3x²−2x+8)(x−3)+28",
            "P(x)=(3x²+2x+8)(x−3)−28",
            "P(x)=(3x²+2x−8)(x−3)+28"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "hint": "Use synthetic division with 3; the final value is the remainder.",
          "steps": [
            {
              "explain": "Use the coefficients 3,−7,2,4 and synthetic value 3.",
              "work": "3 | 3  −7  2  4"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Bring down and multiply-add across.",
              "work": "3; then 2; then 8; remainder 28"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Read quotient and remainder.",
              "work": "Q(x)=3x²+2x+8; R=28"
            }
          ],
          "keyPoints": [
